 ],
 "literal": "O gentle-natured one! O gentle-natured one! / Our dark beauty, free from blame, which has lost its good modesty, / other than enduring with fortitude, if we speak, / can words express it, O gentle-natured one? / In the very town where both the small and the great live, / without a day's interval, of the flood of abundant water, / like a big tree on the firm bank, / we shall embrace many times indeed in a state free of harm.",
 "translation": "O gentle friend, O gentle friend! Our flawless dark beauty has lost its fine modesty. Other than bearing this with fortitude, if we try to speak of it, can words ever express our grief, O gentle friend? In this town where both the small-minded and the noble live, like a great tree standing on the firm bank of a river whose abundant waters flood without a single day's pause, we shall embrace him many times, in a state free of any harm.",
 "modern": "மென்மையான இயல்புடைய தோழியே! மென்மையான இயல்புடைய தோழியே! நல்ல நாணத்தை இழந்த, குற்றமற்ற நம் மாமை நிறத்துத் துன்பத்தை, மனவலிமையோடு பொறுத்துக் கொள்வதைத் தவிர, வாய்திறந்து சொன்னால் சொற்களால் அதனை விவரிக்க முடியுமா, மென்மையான இயல்புடைய தோழியே? அறிவில் சிறியோரும் பெரியோரும் வாழ்கின்ற இந்த ஊரிலே, நாள்களுக்கு இடையே இடைவெளி இல்லாமல் எப்போதும் பெருகி ஓடும் குளிர்ந்த நீர்ப் பெருக்கினைக் கொண்ட ஆற்றின் திண்ணிய கரையில் நிற்கும் பெரிய மரத்தைப் போல, நாம் எவ்விதத் தீங்கும் இல்லாத நன்னிலையில் தலைவனைப் பலமுறை தழுவி இன்புறுவோம்.",
 "explanation": "The heroine is speaking to her close friend (தோழி) to reassure her of her resilience and hope during a period of separation. She notes that her beautiful dark skin has lost its luster and modesty due to the pain of separation, and that words cannot fully express her suffering. However, she expresses confidence that their love will endure. Just like a massive tree on a strong riverbank remains steadfast despite the unceasing, heavy floods, she and her lover will overcome the gossip of the town (where both small-minded and noble people live) and embrace each other many times in a safe, faultless state. The 'flood of abundant water' represents the relentless passage of time or the constant stream of gossip (alar) from the townspeople, while the 'firm bank' represents their unwavering virtue and mutual love. This imagery belongs to the Marutam landscape, symbolizing domestic stability and overcoming marital discord or separation. Key words include 'மெல்லியலோயே' (O gentle-natured friend), 'மாமை' (dark beauty of skin), 'முயங்குகம்' (we shall embrace), and 'திண்கரைப் பெருமரம்' (big tree on a firm bank).",
